# Repo-root .dockerignore
#
# Per V11 EPIC-008-F-004 S-002-REQ-T-001 + BUG-003 #1, local backend Docker
# builds use the REPO ROOT as the build context (so Dockerfiles can COPY
# sibling-tree paths like Code/Shared/, Code/evaluate_care/, brain/, etc.).
# Without this file, Docker would ship the entire 250+ MB tree to the daemon
# every build.
#
# Per Docker docs (https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/):
# "Excluded patterns are removed from the build context before it's sent
#  to the builder."
#
# Keep the list narrow: exclude only what is large or definitely unwanted.
# Anything an individual Dockerfile needs MUST NOT be excluded here.

# Version control + IDE noise
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Python build/cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv

# Node build/cache (the React frontend dist is rebuilt on the host before
# Docker runs and copied into Code/.../backend/static/, so the container
# pulls the static assets via a normal COPY of backend/static/)
**/node_modules
**/.vite
**/.next
**/dist

# Claude / agent outputs
test_output
claude_thoughts
gpt_thoughts

# Docker leftovers
**/Dockerfile.bak
**/.dockerignore

# Local secrets — Code/.env is mounted at runtime via `-e` env-args, never
# baked into the image
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Large repo-root artifacts not used by any container build
Analysis
Legal
LangGraph
docs
enrichment_content
findCare
*.png
*.bak
migrate_progress.log
